WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:03.679
I'm not going to do this to you even every
week.

00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:06.250
Never mind every day for the next two years.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:12.110
But because last night failed, former President
Donald Trump announced another run for president

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.849
in 2024.

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:20.019
We have to look at what the polling says right
now, not only about Trump versus other Republicans,

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.130
but also general election polling.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:28.039
I was telling you earlier, we have a very
different situation now for Trump's run than

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:30.290
we did in 2016 or 2020.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:34.320
Now, Donald Trump, number one, has become
a clear loser.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.079
2018 wasn't great for Republicans.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:42.660
2020 was a disaster for Trump and Republicans,
and 2022 was the red wave that I guess could

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.000
have been but wasn't for Republicans.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.800
And so now you have a Republican electorate
not completely sick of and tired of Trump,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.680
but certainly much more so than in years past.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.650
And you have a guy that is very well-liked
among Republicans, and that is Ron DeSantis,

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:03.010
the governor of Florida, who was just reelected
by a 19 nearly 20 point margin.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.580
That is a blowout win for Ron DeSantis.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.670
We don't yet know the impact of last night's
announcement that Donald Trump is running

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.000
on the polling.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:16.450
But we do have a bunch of polls released after
the November 8th midterms and they're very

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.850
bad for Donald Trump.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:18.850
Let's take a look at this.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:24.350
You can find this on the 538 Republican primary,
2024 page.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:30.170
And what we see is that there is a seven letter
insight poll released today that shows Ron

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.229
DeSantis plus eight over Donald Trump still
with a lot of undecideds.

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:40.090
We do have a single morning consult poll from
yesterday that still shows Trump ahead by

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:41.340
14 over DeSantis.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:48.250
But then we have a CWC Research poll looking
at Texas, which has DeSantis plus 11 over

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:53.329
Donald Trump in Georgia, Florida, New Hampshire
and Iowa.

00:01:53.329 --> 00:01:59.170
WPA intelligence polls, which are okay, they're
rated A, B, C by FiveThirtyEight.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.810
All have Ron DeSantis ahead between plus 11
and plus 26.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:10.550
We have a larger poll of the national Republican
primary which has the Santos at plus two.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:15.410
And then we have a YouGov poll which is the
best ranked pollster of all of these at a

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:19.349
B-plus with Ron DeSantis plus seven.

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:22.140
Ron DeSantis plus seven.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.099
This is a very different situation than in
years past.

00:02:27.099 --> 00:02:34.980
We will maybe know by Monday, maybe next Tuesday
or Wednesday what the polling looks like after

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.170
Trump's announcement.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.690
Will Trump's announcement help him in that
it will invigorate people to say, okay, DeSantis

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:41.690
isn't even running.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.500
Trump's running, I'm throwing my support behind
Trump.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:50.080
Or will Trump's early announcement, which
was ill advised, according to many right wing

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.900
strategists, actually hurt Trump?

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.370
That would be an interesting thing to see.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.620
Now, also notable and again, I'm not going
to do this to you every day or even every

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.490
week for the next two years.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:05.799
If we look at general election polls for 2024
and it is so early, but it is still interesting

00:03:05.799 --> 00:03:13.180
if you look at a new poll released by Leger,
again, a, b, c pollster in a hypothetical

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:17.060
Biden versus Trump matchup, it is Biden plus
three.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.470
And in a hypothetical Biden versus DeSantis
matchup, it is the Santos plus two.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.330
In that poll, DeSantis polling way better.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:32.140
And then in a bunch of different Biden polls
for 2024 from morning consult it is Biden

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.819
winning in every single one.

00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:35.730
It's Biden defeating Christie.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.730
Cheney.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:37.730
Pompeo.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:38.730
Rick Scott.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:39.730
Hogan, Noam.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:40.730
Tim Scott.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.730
Tom Cotton Hawley.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:42.730
Cruz.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:43.730
Haley.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:44.730
Romney.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:45.730
Rubio.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:46.730
Pence.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:47.730
The best outcome is DeSantis.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:52.569
DeSantis is the only one that in that poll
is even even with Joe Biden.

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:56.880
And then this one from right before the election,
actually, this is from New York.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.390
New York is a very blue state, kind of meaningless.

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:00.390
Okay.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.920
So the other point here is.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:08.810
Trump and other Republicans, short of Ron
DeSantis, aren't even polling well in hypothetical

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.140
matchups against Joe Biden.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.410
Joe Biden also hasn't announced that he's
running in 2024.

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:16.940
So a very different situation here.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:23.040
We are taking a picture right now and then
we're going to give it six or so months and

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.010
see how things are looking in the spring.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:28.640
But it is not at all clear.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.360
Even though many Republicans insist this nomination
is Trump's for the taking, it is not clear

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.570
that it is really Trump's for the taking.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:40.700
And it is not at all clear that if Trump wins
that nomination that he is in a strong position

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.570
to actually win in 2024.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.380
At which point, by the way, he will be, you
know, nearly 80 years old.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.940
And that's a whole other story which we will
get to.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:54.419
The point is this could all end in genuine
historic humiliation for Donald Trump

